{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790277661,"nonce":"r5xEP+tu6+a+CIXtoP3swYj2/XQ=","title":"Python: a list comprehension calling a method of None panics in lowering","message":"A list comprehension whose element calls an attribute of a value typed None is not typed as a list, and lowering reaches `unreachable!()` in the ListComp arm of `expr` (lower.rs, `let Ty::List(elem) = ty else { unreachable!() }`). Same on main dea6d08b and on the p2 branch; a plain call `o.attr(1)` outside a comprehension raises AttributeError correctly.\n\n```python\no = None\nprint([o.attr(v) for v in []])\n```\n\nCPython prints `[]` (the element never runs). zypy: `thread main panicked ... internal error: entered unreachable code`, rc 101. With a non-empty iterable CPython raises AttributeError. The comprehension should be typed List(Object) whatever its element types as, and the element should raise at run time.","files":null}]}